# How many Earths fit between Earth and the Moon?
subtitle: "Guess how many Earths would fill the gap to the Moon, then watch all the other planets squeeze into the same gap, drawn to scale."
voices: {"a":"gemini:Enceladus | an awed space quiz host; breathy wonder, but keep moving","take":"lines"}
format: quiz

## How many Earths fit between Earth and the Moon?
affirm: playful
text: {"font_size":32}
sources:
    - id: nasa
      title: Planetary Fact Sheet
      authors: NASA Goddard Space Flight Center
      year: 2024
      url: https://nssdc.gsfc.nasa.gov/planetary/factsheet/
      finding: average Earth-Moon distance 384,400 km; Earth's diameter 12,756 km; equatorial and polar diameters of the planets (Jupiter 142,984 / 133,708 km)

